Z||000004||mrfiero||09-08-2001||04:26 PM||||$30 million over 10 years really isn't a whole lot......I agree there shouldn't be that much waste, but in the grand scheme of things it is a very small percentage of the <B>billions</B> of dollars that get distributed each year through Social Security.<P>The main reason we won't have any money in 30 years is everyone keeps dipping into the cookie jar.  Anytime the government needs cash they raid the bulging wallet of the social security administration. A good example is what we are experiencing now......thanks to dubya's "tax rebate" crap our small surplus has been largely depleted and now, to pay the bills, they need to tap into the social security reserves.  <P>This happens time and time again.  If the gov't never raided these funds there would be untold billions in the coffers waiting to be claimed when we all retire.<P>To add salt to the wound, the first wave of baby boomers will be retiring soon....this will compound the problem and will wreak havoc on the system.  Watch for a major overhaul within the next 10-15 years.<P>Also (and a little bit off topic), watch for the big "R" to hit us very soon.  I think 2002 will be brutal for the US.....a recession is upon us!  Dubya will get blamed (that tax rebate will come back to haunt him), but in reality the ball was rolling when Bubba was still in power....LONG before Dubya took office.<P>Enjoy it while you can!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>         ||||reg||1
